  "text": "And whoever owns the century. The world is one continuous puzzle in which no piece is the thing it depicts. Nothing marks a horizon. A single bone-colored form stands on an endless tan desert under a sourceless amber light, its surface pitted and stacked like something grown by accretion rather than built. Small stalks and pebble-shapes cast long thin shadows around its base, each shadow pointing a slightly different direction as though lit by several suns at once. And whoever owns the century. One sliver dropped in a glass becomes a spreading white stone within seconds.",
